flowchart TB
accTitle: Direct cross-account requests require both accounts to authorize access
accDescr: The caller keeps its existing identity. Caller identity permissions and the target resource policy both authorize the operation, while Config separately evaluates policy configuration.
subgraph CALL[Caller account]
P[Existing caller credentials]:::inputData --> I[Identity policy allows operation]:::reference
end
subgraph OWNER[Resource account]
R[Bucket, key or domain policy<br/>Allows approved external principal]:::reference
C[AWS Config managed or custom check]:::process -.->|Evaluate configuration| R
end
I --> A{Both sides allow<br/>No applicable explicit deny?}:::decision
R --> A
A -->|Yes| O[Supported cross-account operation]:::output
A -->|No| X[Access denied]:::error
